## 2. User stories & acceptance criteria
<%#hasWeb%>
- **AC-001** Given the web app is running, when a user opens the web root `/`, then the page shows the greeting `Hello, World!`.
- **AC-002** Given the web app is running, when a user opens `/?name=Ada`, then the page shows the greeting `Hello, Ada!`.
- **AC-003** Given the web app is running, when a user opens `/` with a `name` longer than 50 characters, then the name is ignored and the page shows `Hello, World!`.
<%/hasWeb%>
<%#hasMobile%>
- **<%mobileAc1%>** Given the mobile app has launched, when its first screen shows, then it displays the greeting `Hello, World!`.
- **<%mobileAc2%>** Given the first screen is showing, when the user types `Ada` into the name field, then it displays `Hello, Ada!`.
- **<%mobileAc3%>** Given the first screen is showing, when the user types a name longer than 50 characters, then the name is ignored and the screen shows `Hello, World!`.
<%/hasMobile%>

## 3. Permissions & roles
None: <%#hasWeb%>the page<%#hasMobile%> and the screen are<%/hasMobile%><%^hasMobile%> is<%/hasMobile%><%/hasWeb%><%^hasWeb%>the screen is<%/hasWeb%> public and read-only.

## 4. Data & validation
- `name`: <%#hasWeb%>optional query parameter<%#hasMobile%> on the web page, and the text of the name field in the mobile app<%/hasMobile%><%/hasWeb%><%^hasWeb%>the text of the name field<%/hasWeb%>. Surrounding spaces are removed; it is used only when it is then 1 to 50 characters long. Anything else (missing, blank, longer than 50) is ignored and the greeting is for `World`.
